From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] version: describe tag 1.2 without git history

uavs3d's CMake runs version.sh while configuring, and the script derives
the build number and the commit id from git in the directory CMake runs
it from. Built from an archive of tag 1.2 there is no git history, so the
build number would be 0 (version 1.2.0) and the commit id empty; inside
another repository's work tree, both would describe that repository.

Use fixed values for tag 1.2 instead: build number 1, so version.h holds
VER_BUILD 1, VERSION_STR "1.2.1" and VERSION_TYPE "release" and the
pkg-config version stays 1.2.1, and the tag's commit
0e20d2c291853f196c68922a264bcd8471d75b68 as VERSION_SHA1, the identifier
uavs3d_create prints. Nothing else in the build changes.

Licence: this patch is part of Vivid's Lucid Engine patch series for
uavs3d and is distributed under the same three-clause BSD licence as
uavs3d (BSD-3-Clause).
---
diff --git a/version.sh b/version.sh
--- a/version.sh
+++ b/version.sh
@@ -15,9 +15,12 @@
     shell_dir=$1
 fi
 
-VER_R=`git rev-list origin/master | sort | wc -l | awk '{print $1}'`
-VER_L=`git rev-list HEAD | sort | wc -l | awk '{print $1}'`
-VER_SHA1=`git log -n 1 | head -n 1 | cut -d ' ' -f 2`
+# Built from an archive of tag 1.2, which has no git history to count, so
+# the build number and commit are fixed: version 1.2.1, and the tag's
+# commit as the identifier.
+VER_R=1
+VER_L=1
+VER_SHA1=0e20d2c291853f196c68922a264bcd8471d75b68
 
 major_version="1"
 minor_version="2"
